---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Market Value vs Replacement Cost | Unitech Accident Assessor"
  description="Understand the difference between market value and replacement cost in Kenyan vehicle valuation and insurance contexts."
  pageTitle="Market Value vs Replacement Cost"
>
  <main class="page-main">
    <section class="content-section">
      <div class="content-grid">
        <article class="article-card">
          <p class="article-lead">
            Market value and replacement cost both describe what a vehicle is worth, but they are
            used for different financial and insurance decisions.
          </p>

          <h2>Market value</h2>
          <p>
            Market value is the amount your vehicle would likely sell for in the current Kenyan
            market. It reflects age, mileage, condition, popularity, and current demand for similar
            units.
          </p>

          <h2>Replacement cost</h2>
          <p>
            Replacement cost is the amount needed to replace the vehicle with a new or equivalent
            unit at today’s prices. Unlike market value, it does not deduct depreciation.
          </p>

          <h2>Which one do insurers usually use in Kenya?</h2>
          <p>
            Most Kenyan insurance settlements are based on market value, especially for used
            vehicles. Replacement cost is more common for new, high-value, agreed-value, or select
            commercial policies.
          </p>

          <h2>When each approach is useful</h2>
          <div class="comparison-grid">
            <div class="mini-card">
              <h3>Use market value for</h3>
              <ul class="content-list">
                <li>Insurance claims</li>
                <li>Buying or selling used cars</li>
                <li>Court or succession matters</li>
                <li>Loan collateral review</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="mini-card">
              <h3>Use replacement cost for</h3>
              <ul class="content-list">
                <li>Brand-new vehicle cover</li>
                <li>Special fleet arrangements</li>
                <li>Rare or high-value vehicles</li>
                <li>Asset replacement planning</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <aside class="sidebar-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Important note</p>
          <h2>Policy wording decides compensation.</h2>
          <p>
            Before relying on replacement cost, always check the insurer’s actual policy wording or
            have a valuer explain the coverage basis.
          </p>
          <a class="button button--primary" href="https://wa.me/254755668653" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            Ask on WhatsApp
          </a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</MainLayout>
